  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「セイヨウナツユキソウ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%BB%E3%82%A4%E3%83%A8%E3%82%A6%E3%83%8A%E3%83%84%E3%83%A6%E3%82%AD%E3%82%BD%E3%82%A6",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 106505550,
      "text": "セイヨウナツユキソウ（Filipendula ulmaria・日本語表記でフィリペンドゥラ・ウルマリア\n)は、バラ科シモツケソウ属の多年草。英名はメドウスイート(meadowsweet)。漢字では「西洋夏雪草」と書く。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Filipendula ulmaria」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Filipendula_ulmaria",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1344915470,
      "text": "Filipendula ulmaria, commonly known as meadowsweet or mead wort, is a perennial herbaceous plant in the family Rosaceae that grows in damp meadows. It is native throughout most of Europe and Western Asia. It has been introduced and naturalised in North America."
    }
